== 10.8 Chapter 10 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [A microscope has a ×10 eyepiece and a ×40 objective. Its total magnification is],
  [×4000],
  [×50],
  [×4],
  [×400]
)

#mcq(2, [The part of the microscope that holds the slide is the],
  [body tube],
  [stage],
  [arm],
  [condenser]
)

#mcq(3, [The coarse adjustment knob should be used only with],
  [the condenser],
  [the low-power objective],
  [the eyepiece],
  [the highest-power objective]
)

#mcq(4, [A microscope should be carried by the],
  [body tube],
  [arm and base],
  [stage],
  [eyepiece]
)

#mcq(5, [The image seen through a light microscope is],
  [exactly as the object],
  [inverted and reversed],
  [upside down but not reversed],
  [upright and the right way round]
)

#mcq(6, [The reagent used to test for starch is],
  [Biuret solution],
  [ethanol],
  [iodine solution],
  [Benedict's solution]
)

#mcq(7, [Benedict's solution gives a brick-red colour with],
  [starch],
  [protein],
  [a reducing sugar],
  [fat]
)

#mcq(8, [Benedict's test must be carried out],
  [in a freezer],
  [in a boiling water bath],
  [at room temperature],
  [over a naked flame]
)

#mcq(9, [Biuret solution gives a purple colour with],
  [protein],
  [a reducing sugar],
  [fat],
  [starch]
)

#mcq(10, [The emulsion test is used for],
  [vitamin C],
  [protein],
  [starch],
  [fat]
)

#mcq(11, [The independent variable in an experiment is the one that],
  [is deliberately changed],
  [is kept constant],
  [is measured],
  [is ignored]
)

#mcq(12, [A control in an experiment is used to],
  [make the results more colourful],
  [show that the result is due to the variable being tested],
  [increase the number of readings],
  [make the experiment take longer]
)

#mcq(13, [Which instrument would be most suitable for measuring the mass of a small seedling accurately?],
  [A beam balance],
  [A metre rule],
  [A measuring cylinder],
  [A thermometer]
)

#mcq(14, [The part of the microscope that controls the amount of light passing through the specimen is the],
